# 64 GB tier, night 64-5: replication of the cells that decide between the Qwen3.6-35B-A3B 8-bit
# and Occamy 4-bit (plan.md §5.3, design §7 rule 2), at 48 GB wired, workspace server.
# Run: mise run night-run-3 -- --part local --queue reports/2026-09-26-64gb-tier/night-64-5.queue
#
# 4 runs × 2 tasks = 8 fresh samples per rung per model (64-2 had 4). Order by cell, both models
# per cell, so a short night still finishes whole comparisons: decompose edit-single r3-r5
# (Occamy 12/12 vs 11/12), retry2 create-file r1-r3 (8-bit 11/12 vs 8/12), decompose
# edit-multi r3-r6 (13/16 each). No base steps; Laguna is not a candidate.
# Expected minutes are 64-2's step times doubled; timeouts ~1.7× that.
#
# part kind  classes               variant   runs rungs timeout-min expected-min profile
local lever edit-single           decompose 4    3-5   40          22           qwen3.6-35b-a3b-8bit-64g
local lever edit-single           decompose 4    3-5   45          26           occamy-1.0-4bit-64g
local lever create-file           retry2    4    1-3   165         97           qwen3.6-35b-a3b-8bit-64g
local lever create-file           retry2    4    1-3   220         131          occamy-1.0-4bit-64g
local lever edit-multi-mechanical decompose 4    3-6   135         78           qwen3.6-35b-a3b-8bit-64g
local lever edit-multi-mechanical decompose 4    3-6   140         83           occamy-1.0-4bit-64g
